    {
      "id": "section:1/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Why a slab allocator?",
      "source_hash": 763750634364238270,
      "context_hash": 1081562996832559231,
      "translation": "왜 slab 할당자인가",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "slab allocator": "slab 할당자"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:18:18.016393Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "`kmalloc` could just call the page allocator for every allocation, but that's wasteful:",
      "source_hash": 517864138037619766,
      "context_hash": 14613055165634018035,
      "translation": "`kmalloc`가 모든 할당마다 페이지 할당자를 직접 호출할 수도 있지만, 이는 낭비입니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "page allocator": "페이지 할당자"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:18:18.016393Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "Page allocator minimum granularity: 4096 bytes",
      "source_hash": 18310479082468841362,
      "context_hash": 2035487978310484895,
      "translation": "페이지 할당자의 최소 할당 단위: 4096바이트",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "bytes": "바이트",
        "page allocator": "페이지 할당자"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:18:18.016394Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "Typical kernel allocation: 32–512 bytes",
      "source_hash": 15228477404540648161,
      "context_hash": 18296998304399066188,
      "translation": "일반적인 커널 할당 크기: 32–512바이트",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "bytes": "바이트",
        "kernel": "커널"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:18:18.016395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "Objects of the same type are created and freed repeatedly",
      "source_hash": 2010220266565861204,
      "context_hash": 16552797431151790886,
      "translation": "같은 타입의 객체가 반복적으로 생성되고 해제됨",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:18:18.016395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "The slab allocator solves this by:",
      "source_hash": 12020934534419232583,
      "context_hash": 12184363791983326048,
      "translation": "slab 할당자는 다음과 같은 방법으로 이 문제를 해결합니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "slab allocator": "slab 할당자"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:18:18.016395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:6/seg:0",
      "source": "Allocating objects from pre-divided pages (\"slabs\")",
      "source_hash": 12529253604281452087,
      "context_hash": 8268025269316189080,
      "translation": "미리 분할해 둔 페이지(\"slab\")에서 객체 할당",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "slabs": "slab"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:18:18.016395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:7/seg:0",
      "source": "Caching freed objects for immediate reuse (no page allocator round-trip)",
      "source_hash": 16009103030723728826,
      "context_hash": 15728198327855247616,
      "translation": "해제된 객체를 즉시 재사용할 수 있도록 캐싱(페이지 할당자 왕복 없음)",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "page allocator": "페이지 할당자"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:18:18.016395Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:8/seg:0",
      "source": "Exploiting constructor patterns: objects are often the same type",
      "source_hash": 16057327959101996385,
      "context_hash": 7001459693266919441,
      "translation": "생성자 패턴 활용: 객체는 대개 같은 타입임",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:18:18.016396Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:9/seg:0",
      "source": "Linux uses **SLUB** (the \"unqueued\" slab allocator) since 2.6.23.",
      "source_hash": 9337742911905989948,
      "context_hash": 11200017580156732667,
